## Testing approach

Prefer tests at the outermost meaningful boundary. Protect externally observable contracts without coupling tests to private implementation details. Use realistic fixtures or fakes rather than mocks of internal call choreography. Use lower-level tests only when they are needed to cover unusually risky internals.

## Responsibility

Establish the repository baseline and implement only the tests required by the approved plan. Do not implement the feature behavior.

